{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","title":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields.md","line":30,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields.tex#prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#def:pet-ch8-killing-field]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields.tex","label":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","line":47,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[covariant-derivative criterion]\n  \\label{prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0328}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch8-killing-field, prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative}\n  \\dcref{ch8:8.1.2}\n  A vector field $X$ is a Killing field if and only if $v\\mapsto\\nabla_vX$ is a\n  skew-symmetric $(1,1)$-tensor, i.e.\\ $g(\\nabla_vX,w)=-g(\\nabla_wX,v)$ for all\n  $v,w$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric}\n  \\sketch\n  Metric compatibility and torsion-freeness give\n  \\[\n    (L_Xg)(V,W)=g(\\nabla_VX,W)+g(V,\\nabla_WX).\n  \\]\n  Hence \\cref{prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative} identifies the Killing\n  equation with skew-adjointness of the endomorphism \\(V\\mapsto\\nabla_VX\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[covariant-derivative criterion] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368382d6b696c6c696e672d736b65772d73796d6d6574726963\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0328</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_KillingFields%23def%3Apet-ch8-killing-field\">↗ def:pet-ch8-killing-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_KillingFields%23prop%3Apet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative\">↗ prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch8:8.1.2</span></span>A vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> is a Killing field if and only if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\mapsto \\nabla _vX$\">$v\\mapsto \\nabla _vX$</span> is a skew-symmetric <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(1,1)$\">$(1,1)$</span>-tensor, i.e. <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g(\\nabla _vX,w)=-g(\\nabla _wX,v)$\">$g(\\nabla _vX,w)=-g(\\nabla _wX,v)$</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v,w$\">$v,w$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_KillingFields%23prop%3Apet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric\">↗ prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric</a> \\sketch Metric compatibility and torsion-freeness give </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (L_Xg)(V,W)=g(\\nabla _VX,W)+g(V,\\nabla _WX).  \\]\">\\[  (L_Xg)(V,W)=g(\\nabla _VX,W)+g(V,\\nabla _WX).  \\]</span></p><p> Hence <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_KillingFields%23prop%3Apet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a7065742d6368382d6b696c6c696e672d6c69652d64657269766174697665\">section 1</a> identifies the Killing equation with skew-adjointness of the endomorphism <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V\\mapsto \\nabla _VX$\">$V\\mapsto \\nabla _VX$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-curvature-identities","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#def:pet-ch8-killing-field","title":"def:pet-ch8-killing-field","label":"def:pet-ch8-killing-field"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative","title":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative","label":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-lie-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","title":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","label":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","title":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric","label":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-skew-symmetric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#prop:pet-ch8-killing-uniqueness","title":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-uniqueness","label":"prop:pet-ch8-killing-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_KillingFields#thm:pet-ch8-zero-set-totally-geodesic","title":"thm:pet-ch8-zero-set-totally-geodesic","label":"thm:pet-ch8-zero-set-totally-geodesic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"refer